+# 01: Import a clean file into an empty contactbook
+
+**What to build:** The tracer bullet for CSV Import. A caller hands `import_contacts` the text of a valid file in the Export format, and each row becomes a new Contact. The Import report lists the emails created. A file that can't be imported at all because it's empty or is missing the name or email column raises `ImportFileError` and changes nothing. See the spec: `.scratch/csv-import/spec.md`.
+
+This ticket lays down the fixed interface: `import_contacts(repo, data)`, `ImportReport` (`created`, `updated`, `errors`, `warnings`), `RowIssue` (`row`, `column`, `message`) and `ImportFileError(ContactError)`. Later tickets fill in the behaviour.
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] `import_contacts`, `ImportReport` and `RowIssue` live in a new importer module with exactly the signatures in the spec. `ImportFileError` derives from `ContactError` in the errors module.
+- [ ] `ImportFileError` can be imported from the package root alongside the other domain errors, and the README layout lists the importer module.
+- [ ] Text input with the header `name,email,phone,tags` and valid rows creates one Contact per row, with values normalised by the existing validators (e.g. `Ann@Example.COM` stored as `ann@example.com`, phone formatting stripped, tags split on `;`).
+- [ ] `created` lists the normalised emails in file order. `updated`, `errors` and `warnings` are empty.
+- [ ] A file with no content (empty or whitespace-only) raises `ImportFileError` saying the file is empty.
+- [ ] A header without a `name` or `email` column raises `ImportFileError` naming the missing column.
+- [ ] A header with no data rows returns an empty `ImportReport` and raises no error.
+- [ ] Whenever `ImportFileError` is raised, the repository is unchanged. Checking happens before anything is written.
+- [ ] Passing something that is neither `str` nor `bytes` raises `TypeError`. Accepting `bytes` comes later, in ticket 08.
+- [ ] Tests go through `import_contacts` only, using inline CSVs, in the style of the existing pytest files.
+
+## Comments
+
+Implemented on integration branch `csv-import` (merged in 81f5494; code-review fixes in 85880f7). Tests: `tests/test_import*.py`.
