+# 02: Merge rows into existing Contacts
+
+**What to build:** When a row's email already belongs to a Contact, the Import updates that Contact instead of failing. The row's name replaces the stored name. A blank phone keeps the stored phone and a filled-in phone replaces it. The row's tags are added to the stored ones and never removed. The Import report lists such emails under `updated`, but only when the Contact actually changed, so re-importing an Export reports nothing. See "Applying a valid row" in `.scratch/csv-import/spec.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Import a clean file into an empty contactbook)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] A row whose email matches a stored Contact (case-insensitively, after trimming) updates that Contact through the repository. No duplicate is created.
+- [ ] The stored name is replaced by the row's name.
+- [ ] A blank phone cell keeps the stored phone. A valid non-blank phone replaces it.
+- [ ] The row's tags are added to the stored tags. Stored tags missing from the row are kept.
+- [ ] The normalised email appears in `updated` (in file order) only if the merged Contact differs from the stored one.
+- [ ] A row that changes nothing appears in neither `created` nor `updated` and produces no warning.
+- [ ] Exporting a repository with the existing CSV export and importing the result back into the same repository gives an empty report and leaves the repository unchanged.
+- [ ] A file that mixes new and existing emails fills both `created` and `updated` correctly.
+
+## Comments
+
+Implemented on integration branch `csv-import` (merged in 392b86c; code-review fixes in 85880f7). Tests: `tests/test_import*.py`.
