+# 03: Reject invalid rows with row errors
+
+**What to build:** A row with a missing or invalid email, name or tag is rejected. It is skipped entirely and reported as Row errors, while the valid rows in the same file are still imported. Every invalid field in the row is reported at once, each with the row number and the column, so Sales can fix the whole row in one pass. A rejected row never changes anything, not even part of an existing Contact. Tags are split on `;` only. See "Field rules" in `.scratch/csv-import/spec.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Import a clean file into an empty contactbook)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] Missing or invalid email → Row error with `column="email"`. Missing or invalid name → `column="name"`. Any invalid tag → `column="tags"`.
+- [ ] Each invalid field produces exactly one `RowIssue`, whose message is the validator's message (without the field name). All invalid fields in a row are reported, not just the first.
+- [ ] `RowIssue.row` is the spreadsheet row number: header = 1, first data row = 2. Blank-row and multi-line handling come in ticket 06.
+- [ ] A rejected row is not applied: no new Contact, and an existing Contact with that email is left completely unchanged.
+- [ ] Valid rows in the same file are still created or updated as normal.
+- [ ] A blank name is a Row error even when the email belongs to an existing Contact. It never means "keep the stored name".
+- [ ] The tags cell is split on `;` only. Pieces are trimmed, empty pieces dropped (`vip; ;prospect;` → two tags), and repeats collapse after normalisation (`vip;VIP` → one tag).
+- [ ] A tag containing a comma (`vip, prospect`) is an invalid tag, so the row is rejected.
+- [ ] `errors` are in row order.
+
+## Comments
+
+Implemented on integration branch `csv-import` (merged in 2f54ea2; code-review fixes in 85880f7). Tests: `tests/test_import*.py`.
