+# 05: Duplicate emails within a file
+
+**What to build:** When the same Contact appears twice in one file (same email after normalisation), only the first row counts. Every later row with that email is a Row error pointing back at the first row, so Sales can see and resolve the duplication. Whether a row is a duplicate depends only on the file, not on whether the first copy was imported. See "Duplicate emails within the file" in `.scratch/csv-import/spec.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** 03 (Reject invalid rows with row errors)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] Rows are compared by normalised email (`Ann@x.com` on row 5 and ` ann@x.com` on row 40 are the same).
+- [ ] The first row with a given email is processed normally. Every later row with it gets a Row error with `column="email"` whose message refers to the first row's number (e.g. "duplicate of row 5"), and is not applied.
+- [ ] If the first row is itself rejected (e.g. bad tag), later rows with the same email are still duplicate errors, and nothing is imported for that email.
+- [ ] Rows whose email is missing or invalid take no part in duplicate detection.
+- [ ] No email ever appears in both `created` and `updated`, or twice in either list.
+
+## Comments
+
+Implemented on integration branch `csv-import` (merged in b43d90b; code-review fixes in 85880f7). Tests: `tests/test_import*.py`.
