+# 07: Flexible headers and the first_name/last_name pair
+
+**What to build:** Sales can import their spreadsheet as-is. Column names are matched regardless of case, surrounding spaces and order. Phone and tags are optional. Extra columns like `company` are ignored with a warning. Files from the address-book tool, which uses `first_name` and `last_name` instead of `name`, are accepted too. Headers that are ambiguous are rejected as a whole. See "Header rules" in `.scratch/csv-import/spec.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** 03 (Reject invalid rows with row errors)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] Header names are matched case-insensitively with surrounding whitespace trimmed, in any column order (` Email ,NAME` works).
+- [ ] `phone` and `tags` columns are optional. When absent, every row is treated as having them blank.
+- [ ] Each unknown column is ignored, with one Row warning on the header's row: `column=None`, message naming the header as written (e.g. `ignored unknown column "Company"`).
+- [ ] A recognised column appearing twice raises `ImportFileError`, and the repository is unchanged.
+- [ ] `first_name` + `last_name` together are accepted in place of `name`. Each part is trimmed, blank parts are dropped, and the rest is joined with one space (`Cher` + blank → `Cher`).
+- [ ] Both parts blank → Row error on `name` ("is required"). Any name problem from the pair is reported with `column="name"`, never `first_name`/`last_name`.
+- [ ] Only one of `first_name`/`last_name` (with no `name`) counts as a missing name column, so `ImportFileError`.
+- [ ] `name` together with `first_name`/`last_name` raises `ImportFileError` (name given twice).
+
+## Comments
+
+Implemented on integration branch `csv-import` (merged in ad6f8cb; code-review fixes in 85880f7). Tests: `tests/test_import*.py`.
