+# 09: The 1000-row limit
+
+**What to build:** A file may hold at most 1000 contact rows. A bigger file is rejected as a whole with `ImportFileError` and nothing is imported, so people split it rather than end up with a half-loaded sheet. Blank rows don't count, but rows that would be rejected do. See "Row limit" in `.scratch/csv-import/spec.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** 06 (Excel row numbers, blank rows, and short or long rows)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] A file with exactly 1000 non-blank data rows is imported normally.
+- [ ] A file with 1001 or more non-blank data rows raises `ImportFileError` with a message saying the limit is 1000 rows and the file should be split. The repository is unchanged.
+- [ ] Blank rows (including rows of only commas) don't count: 1000 contact rows plus blank rows is accepted.
+- [ ] Rows that would be rejected (invalid fields, duplicate emails) do count toward the limit.
+- [ ] A file with only a header still returns an empty report.
+
+## Comments
+
+Implemented on integration branch `csv-import` (merged in 5af65b9; code-review fixes in 85880f7). Tests: `tests/test_import*.py`.
diff --git a/.scratch/csv-import/spec.md b/.scratch/csv-import/spec.md
