+# contactbook
+
+The core of the contacts service: who we keep in touch with, and how contacts get in and out of it.
+
+## Language
+
+### Contacts
+
+**Contact**:
+A person we keep in touch with, identified by their email address (compared case-insensitively).
+_Avoid_: Lead, person, entry
+
+### Import and export
+
+**Export**:
+The CSV file contactbook produces from its contacts: one row per Contact with the columns name, email, phone and tags.
+
+**Import**:
+Loading a whole CSV file of contacts in a single action, adding new Contacts and updating existing ones by email.
+_Avoid_: Upload, bulk add
+
+**Import report**:
+The account of what one Import did: which Contacts were created, which were updated, and every row error and row warning.
+
+**Row error**:
+A problem that stops a row from being imported. A rejected row changes nothing, not even part of an existing Contact.
+_Avoid_: Failure
+
+**Row warning**:
+A problem with a row that was still imported, where part of the row was ignored or dropped.
